Z||000013||fierospeeder||11-29-2001||12:34 AM||||i wouldn't buy a car from ebay unless it was in my state and i could look at it.<P><BR>otherwise if it was a 100 dollar beater, then why not.  <P>||||reg||1
Z||000014||Nashco||11-29-2001||02:00 AM||||I bought my GT on ebay.  Seller supplied a ton of pictures, answered EVERY question I had, guaranteed its condition in that if I wasn't satisfied it met descriptions I could get my deposit back and no deal would be made.  I ended up getting it, for about 700-1000 bucks less than the going rate has been!!!  I took a 12 hour greyhound ride up to Indiana and drove it all the way home, even in a little snow <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I had a couple VERY minor catches, but all was well (headlight motor stopped working the day before I showed up, understandable.  Also needed to add a little oil to engine and tranny, as well as overflow coolant and washer fluid <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">).  If the price is right and the seller is very honest and diligent, I say go for it!<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000015||artherd||11-29-2001||05:06 AM||||My T-top car was an ebay-list! He also posted it to several Fiero mailing lists, and it was registered with fierottop.com, so a little more into the cars than your average joe. Seller had it on at $5k-min, got no bids.  I emailed him and asked if he'd take slightly less, he said sure!  About a month later when we lined up our schegule, I *FLEW* out, one way, from SF to Denver, CO.<P>Drove back nearly 1400miles (took the senic route up and down the rockies, hey, as long as I'm there in a toppless mid-engine sports car  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Needless to say, the car was everything he made it out to be, even had about 1k fewer miles on it than he had said  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>PS: Eric, if you're out there, the car's in good hands, and you can come visit her anytime you like!<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000016||mrfixit58||11-29-2001||08:25 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Nashco:<BR><B>I bought my GT on ebay.  Seller supplied a ton of pictures, answered EVERY question I had</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Ditto on my blue 87 GT (Third place trophy winner - Street Stock Division - 2001 Spring Daytona Show). I even payed $1000 to have it shipped from northern California to my house near Tampa, Florida. I really all boils down to the reputation of the seller and the answers he gives to your "intelligent" questions. <P><P>------------------<BR>Roy  :D <BR>Just another stock Blue 87 GT   <BR>Suncoast Fieros<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennocksize.JPG">          <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <P><B>JUST ADDED: </B>1988 GT w/ T-Tops, 5-Speed, and Performance Sound.||||reg||1
Z||000017||FastFieros||11-29-2001||01:42 PM||||I am going to commit to this tread as a seller on eBay. Most of the comments are buyers so far.<P>Some of you know I have been buying and selling Fieros for over 6 years now. My previous eBay ID was "Benchshooter". It got turned off due to selling Star Wars DVD's from China. So I had to revert to an ID I had to purchase from a friend that no longer needed his. "Openwheel" is my current ID on Ebay. <P>You have seen my webpages at <A HREF="http://www.fastfieros.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fastfieros.com</A> <P>I mostly sell 88's on ebay with 3.4 conversions that I do myself. I will start 3.8 SC conversions in 4 weeks.<P>If I sell an 87 and below it is priced real right because I usually consider it a parts car. I however do not like to sell parts and ship parts. It is too time consuming.<P>This forum and the other LIST's servers for Fieros in general have alot of tire kickers. However, I am one who likes to chat long hours about Fieros. My approach to sales on the "NET" are email first, then when the questions start coming its time for the phone numbers. I will give my phone number out and request you to call me if you have questions that require what I consider lengthly conversation. 2nd of all if you take the time to call me, you are interested in buying the car I feel like. I have given my number out to 4 people on this one forum for 2 different 88 Fieros I have sold and not a one called me. Those same cars sold on Ebay with no problems for me or the buyer.<P>You Fiero folks are nice and kind, and I thank all of you for being a contact in the Fiero world. I do this as a hobbie and it is not considered a business for me. Its fun. I plan to keep it that way or I will go on to other things.<P>Today I have purchased 93 Fieros. I currently own 37 sitting at my house behind a 8ft fence. I am still having fun  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Loyde||||reg||10
